DirtyPipe (CVE-2022-0847) allows overwriting any file starting at page 0 with arbitrary data under certain conditions (file has SUID bit, appended data after EOF).
1) Heap Feng-Shui: Allocate 32 4k pages via memfd_create(“hole”) and splice() empty buffers into a pipe to align the PIPE_BUF structures in SLUB.
2) Heap grooming: Spray 1000 msg_msg SHM segments (struct msg_msg->m_ts = 0x1000, m_type = MTYPE_SETXATTR) to occupy the kmalloc-4k slab adjacent to msg_msg->next.
3) Exploit Pipe Primitive:  dup2(pipefd[1], target_file_fd) where target_file_fd is /proc/self/exe; write 1 byte at offset 0 using pipe_buffer.sd->offset trick.  The overwrite corrupts msg_msg->next pointer to point into setxattr security namespace.
4) Core Exploit: Overwrite setxattr(“user.dummy”, …) vector with fake cred structure (uid 0, euid 0) via MSG_COPY from shm segment; trigger validate_change() syscall which invokes security_setxattr() in kernel space.
Code snippet (GNU C):
   struct msgbuf { long mtype; char mtext[0x1000]; };
   msgsnd(msqid, &msg, sizeof(msg)-sizeof(long), IPC_NOWAIT);
   msg.mtype = MTYPE_SETXATTR;
   for(i=0;i<32;i++) memcpy(msg.mtext, fake_cred, 0x1000);
   msgsnd(msqid, &msg, 0, IPC_NOWAAT);
Mitigation: Patch to ≥5.16.16; enable SLUB red zoning; use hardened usercopy (CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY=y); deploy kernel page-table isolation (CONFIG_PAGE_TABLE_ISOLATION=y).  Used in 2022 by Storm-0866 during Operation Nobelium.

